## v1.2.0 (2026-06-20)

Release-notes extraction footer-bleed fix (verified-local). MINOR bump because it corrects
shipped example code, not just prose.

- **Bug**: the release-notes extraction regex used the end-anchor `(?=\n## \[|$)`. For the
  **top/most-recent** dated section (the common case — `[Unreleased]` just promoted to vX.Y.Z),
  there is no next `## [` header below it, only the keepachangelog link-reference footer. So
  `.*?` under `re.DOTALL` ran to EOF and absorbed `[Unreleased]: …/compare/…` and
  `[X.Y.Z]: …/releases/tag/…` into the published GitHub Release body. Demonstrated locally with a
  synthetic top-section CHANGELOG fixture: old anchor → body includes the two footer lines; fixed
  anchor → body stops at the last bullet.
- **Fix**: extend the end-anchor to also stop at the first link-reference line:
  `(?=\n## \[|\n\[[^\]]+\]: |$)`. Updated in the Detailed Steps §A step-3 extraction block and the
  Quick-Reference/Results discussion, with an inline comment explaining the footer-bleed rationale.
- Added a Failed Attempts row ("Release notes absorbed the CHANGELOG link-footer"), a Quick
  Reference note, and a Results & Parameters pytest fixture that asserts `compare/` and
  `releases/tag/` are absent from the extracted body (synthetic top-section CHANGELOG).
- The surrounding release workflow remains CI-verified (skill stays `verified-ci`); the regex fix
  itself is **verified-local** via the synthetic fixture — noted as a qualifier in the Overview
  Verification row and the Failed-Attempts lesson.

